+## 2. Apply-coupon service logic
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with validation order (order exists -> PENDING -> no existing coupon -> string code -> coupon exists -> ACTIVE -> validity window -> usage limit -> minimum amount), returning the updated order; verify each rejection with a service/HTTP test asserting the spec's error code
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `computeDiscount` for `FIXED` (capped at order amount) and `PERCENT` (`Math.floor`, capped by `maxDiscountCents`); verify with tests for the spec's worked examples (1500/12000, 5000/300, 20%/12000, 10%/999, capped 50%)
+- [x] 2.3 Perform the order update, redemption insert and `usedCount` increment inside one transaction; verify a rejected application leaves order and `usedCount` unchanged and a successful one increments `usedCount` by exactly 1
+- [x] 2.4 Ensure `now` is read from the injected `Clock` and compared as parsed timestamps; verify with a fixed clock straddling `validFrom`/`validUntil`
+
+## 3. HTTP endpoint
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` (parse id, read `couponCode`, return `200` with the order); verify via `app.request` that a success returns the discounted order body
+- [x] 3.2 Add endpoint tests in a new file (do not modify `tests/orders.test.ts`) covering the success path plus `INVALID_REQUEST`, `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `ORDER_ALREADY_HAS_COUPON`, `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_NOT_ACTIVE`, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`, `COUPON_EXPIRED`, `COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED`, `ORDER_BELOW_MIN_AMOUNT`; verify `npm test` passes
+
+## 4. Final verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test`; verify the pre-existing tests in `tests/orders.test.ts` still pass unmodified
+- [x] 4.2 Run `openspec validate apply-coupon-to-order --strict`; verify the change validates
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change once implementation is reviewed and all tasks above are complete.
